From a02b3b6e126a9fcef1e542c431d47667d8dbf1f1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: GibaxLeGrand <48137851+GibaxLeGrand@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 16:15:17 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 24/24] Runner: the letters the names lack, from Saira (OFL)

The game's names look like New Rodin Bold (Fontworks, not free). Of the
faces tried for the letters the names do not have (B F P Q X Z, 2-9,
! ? _), Saira Italic (SIL Open Font License 1.1; width axis 118, weight
650) is the closest: at the names' size its letters match their mean
width and white. Gibax chose it. The fills are rendered by
work\etiquettes\police_cpp.py saira.

Measured (2 runners, 8 seats, the 8 racers CPUs, SRNP_TAGS=GIBAX,,K-NUX,
AMY_R,,WAVE!,BOB-PIP,TAILSMKR): 8 finishes, 201 checksums equal, 2
divergences in camera fields; the runner's texture is the prototype's
texel for texel in all 8 bands.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/runtime/srnp_labels.cpp | 41 +++++++++++++++++++------------------
 1 file changed, 21 insertions(+), 20 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/runtime/srnp_labels.cpp b/src/runtime/srnp_labels.cpp
index 04898ff..bb72d14 100644
